<rule>
# Debug and Bugfix Workflow

When debugging, fixing bugs, or changing code in response to broken behavior, first provide the user with a pre-change analysis before editing any code.

Required order:
1. State the observed problem.
2. Explain why the problem happens, based on verified code, logs, or runtime behavior.
3. Describe the planned fix and which files/functions will be changed.
4. Only after that, modify code.
5. After the modification, report what changed and how it was verified.

Do not fix code first and explain the bug afterward. The user must see the bug analysis before code changes.

No extra confirmation is required unless there are multiple risky implementation choices, destructive actions, or missing facts that block diagnosis.
</rule>
